From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:38:08 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0305): host follows only its own relay

AC-61, mitigating the AC-5 server limitation. OSS hbbs 1.1.16 forwards a
controller's RequestRelay to the host without a key check, and the stock
host connects to whatever relay it names, so a keyless client that knows
the host's ID could steer the session to a relay it controls.

The host's relay is pinned: the configured relay-server option, else
the relay port on its own rendezvous server (what RemoteSmith's hbbs
advertises, --relay-servers <same host>:21117). A RequestRelay naming
another relay is refused and logged. Where the host picks the relay
itself (punch hole, intranet fallback) it uses the pinned one, never a
different one from hbbs; upstream preferred hbbs's. Direct and LAN
routes involve no relay.

Deployments whose hbbs advertises a relay on another host must set
relay-server on the host.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
